  },
  "exact_uniform_translation_stability": {
    "symbol": "H6(theta)=sum_{j=-2..3}w_j(f)*exp[-i*theta*(j-f)]",
    "p": "p=f(1-f), in[0,1/4]",
    "s": "s=sin^2(theta/2), in[0,1]",
    "identity": "1-|H6|^2=p(p+2)(p+6)*[(8/45)*s^3+(4p/15)*s^4+(16p(p+2)/225)*s^5]",
    "proof": "The rational polynomial identity was independently expanded with exact Fraction arithmetic. Every term is nonnegative; the expression increases with p and s and equals1 at p=1/4,s=1. Thus0<=|H6|<=1 for all f in[0,1] and all theta. The separable XY symbol is the product of two such symbols.",
    "phase_order": "Centred moments1..5 vanish, so attenuation begins at order theta^6 and asymmetric-phase dispersion at order theta^7. M4 retains moments only through degree2; dispersion begins at order theta^3.",
    "half_cell_weights": [
